WEBVTT

00:06.089 --> 00:08.299
[theme music playing]

01:03.229 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:06.983 --> 01:10.779
I want you to prove it to me.
That all humans are corrupt at heart.

01:11.696 --> 01:13.073
That's my first wish.

01:16.326 --> 01:17.660
You've tempted me. Well done.

01:21.039 --> 01:22.957
You would gamble your life away

01:24.375 --> 01:26.127
just to validate the human race?

01:26.211 --> 01:28.463
Wow. [laughs] That's ridiculous.

01:30.840 --> 01:34.719
No matter what's next,
I'm going to make sure you lose.

01:34.803 --> 01:36.805
I'll crush you, mortal.
You're gonna cry so--

01:36.888 --> 01:38.056
Save it for if you do win.

01:39.224 --> 01:40.225
Just wear it.

01:43.186 --> 01:44.854
Let's get started so I can win.

01:46.439 --> 01:47.816
You're following my lead, okay?

01:49.484 --> 01:52.362
Get a move on, mortal.
The spring nights are short.

01:55.198 --> 01:58.576
So, if you have been imprisoned
for 983 years,

01:58.660 --> 02:00.870
why are you the most famous Genie?

02:01.704 --> 02:04.874
I was famous well before
because I dared to defy His orders.

02:04.958 --> 02:06.209
And why did you defy Him?

02:07.377 --> 02:10.171
-You've tempted me. Well done.
-I was tempte-- [clears throat]

02:12.799 --> 02:16.219
I refused to bow to a creation
forged out of clay of all things.

02:16.302 --> 02:17.929
-A coin on the ground.
-Where?

02:19.180 --> 02:20.682
[amusing music plays]

02:22.433 --> 02:24.060
Just tying my shoelaces.

02:25.603 --> 02:26.521
[hums]

02:29.274 --> 02:31.151
No, please take your time.

02:32.026 --> 02:33.945
Take all the time in the world.

02:36.573 --> 02:40.577
I will corrupt you
if it's the last thing I do, you hear?

02:40.660 --> 02:42.829
I'm gonna snap your neck. Yeah?

02:43.580 --> 02:46.499
I'll hang your head
on the doorknob of hell and…

02:47.625 --> 02:48.918
[Im-seon] Ka-young, is that you?

02:51.713 --> 02:52.630
[Iblis] Huh?

02:54.591 --> 02:56.885
Ah, our first human to corrupt.

02:57.635 --> 02:59.512
I'm overdue for an oil change.

03:00.972 --> 03:03.099
I'll swing by this weekend, okay?

03:03.182 --> 03:04.225
Sure. Come by.

03:06.477 --> 03:07.437
Kang Im-seon.

03:07.520 --> 03:10.023
Works at the supermarket.
Wife of Grandma An's son.

03:10.106 --> 03:12.692
Huh. I know that look well.

03:13.443 --> 03:16.154
That's a woman who'd smile
if the world ended tomorrow.

03:16.237 --> 03:17.238
[cell phone chimes]

03:21.451 --> 03:22.535
Gu Bo-gyeong.

03:23.286 --> 03:24.287
Works at the bank.

03:24.871 --> 03:26.164
We went to school together.

03:30.585 --> 03:33.421
Did you get the message
regarding the towel sets from the bank?

03:36.507 --> 03:38.927
Though, I'm sure
you already have nicer ones.

03:42.972 --> 03:45.225
-Going out?
-Just walking. Good night.

03:45.308 --> 03:46.142
Huh?

03:47.310 --> 03:48.228
Ah.

03:54.275 --> 03:56.319
I also know that look well.

03:56.402 --> 03:59.864
One more who would also smile
if the world ended tomorrow.

04:05.078 --> 04:07.205
That's two. Good as corrupted, no?

04:07.872 --> 04:09.249
[dog growls]

04:09.332 --> 04:10.208
-[dog barks]
-[gasps]

04:14.796 --> 04:17.507
Aw. Another look I know well.

04:17.590 --> 04:20.593
-[continues barking]
-What? Do I not look like I belong here?

04:20.677 --> 04:22.178
Is the lamp oil too strong?

04:25.556 --> 04:28.268
Is your hairpin still in?
Why's he barking at you?

04:29.352 --> 04:30.353
Satisfied?

04:30.979 --> 04:34.315
Dogs can perceive the supernatural.
They can see me no matter what.

04:34.399 --> 04:36.276
-Hmm?
-Is that so? Interesting.

04:37.068 --> 04:40.280
Of the neighborhood, he barks at me
the most out of all the dogs.

04:40.363 --> 04:41.614
Oh, yeah?

04:42.198 --> 04:44.742
I suppose that makes you
our special third mortal.

04:45.243 --> 04:46.828
Nice to meet you, little buddy.

04:46.911 --> 04:47.996
[dog whimpers]

04:48.079 --> 04:50.331
What are you doing?
Our deal doesn't apply to dogs.

04:52.458 --> 04:53.459
Sure about that?

04:54.043 --> 04:56.963
You said the first five lives
we encounter, did you not?

04:57.046 --> 05:00.842
"All mortals" means all life-forms.
That's the rule. Wouldn't you agree?

05:00.925 --> 05:02.302
Ki Ka-young and her rules.

05:03.094 --> 05:04.012
[sighs]

05:04.554 --> 05:06.723
THIS WAY TO CHEONGPUNG VILLAGE HALL

05:10.476 --> 05:11.311
Ms. Ki?

05:12.020 --> 05:13.771
Where are you headed this late?

05:13.855 --> 05:15.690
You know better
than to be out alone at night.

05:15.773 --> 05:16.607
[Iblis] Mm?

05:17.358 --> 05:18.776
-Want a ride?
-No.

05:19.569 --> 05:21.863
I'm waiting for someone here.
I'm not alone.

05:26.701 --> 05:27.577
Okay.

05:28.328 --> 05:29.287
See ya.

05:33.541 --> 05:34.375
[Iblis] Huh.

05:34.917 --> 05:36.502
Eom Sang-tae.

05:36.586 --> 05:39.672
His mother is Grandma Sa.
She owns the gamja-tang joint.

05:39.756 --> 05:43.217
Eom Sang-tae is clearly unaware
that the only menace out here is you.

05:43.301 --> 05:44.677
No, he knows.

05:44.761 --> 05:46.763
Everyone knows all about the weird girl.

05:47.805 --> 05:50.224
But he knows nothing at all
about what I know.

05:51.225 --> 05:52.226
[Iblis scoffs]

05:53.936 --> 05:55.354
Ow, you scared me.

05:55.438 --> 05:57.023
-[Iblis] Hmm?
-[sighs in relief]

05:57.940 --> 06:01.611
You're out for a walk
in the middle of the night. Cool.

06:01.694 --> 06:03.488
YouTube still going well?

06:04.363 --> 06:06.908
-And Da-jin is doing okay?
-[man] Da-jin, lock the doors!

06:06.991 --> 06:08.910
Just kidding. [laughs]

06:08.993 --> 06:10.078
-Okay.
-[Iblis scoffs]

06:10.161 --> 06:11.829
-Have a good night.
-[Iblis scoffs]

06:11.913 --> 06:12.872
[man panting]

06:16.292 --> 06:19.337
I think it's been a year.

06:19.420 --> 06:21.339
He got married and started a farm.

06:21.422 --> 06:23.674
He makes these YouTube videos
with his wife.

06:24.467 --> 06:26.219
That means we have our five.

06:27.011 --> 06:28.137
You must win at least three.

06:28.221 --> 06:30.098
I will make it with all five.

06:31.390 --> 06:34.185
Won't be long
before they've sunk to rock bottom.

06:36.270 --> 06:37.939
And that bottom goes quite deep.

06:38.022 --> 06:40.608
If you ever want to see behind the mask,

06:42.068 --> 06:43.903
just present them with wishes.

06:45.154 --> 06:45.988
Really?

06:46.614 --> 06:49.242
Well, I made a wish.
What's behind my own mask, then?

06:50.159 --> 06:51.577
A psychopath.

06:53.788 --> 06:57.041
Four humans, one dog, all damned.
Thanks to your one wish.

06:58.751 --> 06:59.585
Oh…

07:00.336 --> 07:02.255
I should also mention one other thing.

07:03.172 --> 07:06.134
There are good genies
and there are bad genies in the world.

07:06.968 --> 07:09.887
One, just one can produce hell on Earth.

07:10.763 --> 07:13.641
They call that genie "Iblis"

07:14.392 --> 07:16.811
or "Shaytan" sometimes.

07:17.645 --> 07:20.106
To use a language you'll recognize…

07:22.316 --> 07:23.317
"Satan."

07:27.488 --> 07:28.489
Well…

07:31.033 --> 07:33.035
It appears I've met an evil genie.

07:33.786 --> 07:35.788
[birds cawing and fluttering]

07:36.789 --> 07:38.708
[rats squeaking]

07:40.376 --> 07:42.420
[captivating music playing]

07:42.503 --> 07:44.130
[laughing]

07:49.469 --> 07:51.304
[continues laughing]

07:55.183 --> 07:56.100
[gasps]

08:04.984 --> 08:07.111
[captivating music continues]

08:25.129 --> 08:26.547
[Sade] What are you gonna do now?

08:26.631 --> 08:29.383
Even in this life,
she used a wish for the sake of others.

08:30.259 --> 08:32.595
It's not for the sake of others,
not really.

08:32.678 --> 08:35.181
Did she not just wager her life
on humans being good?

08:35.264 --> 08:38.100
What do you call that?
And what did you say? "Psychopath"?

08:38.184 --> 08:40.311
"I'm Satan"? Oh, yeah. Great job.

08:40.394 --> 08:43.314
Who'd have thought rats
would be so reliable in relaying info?

08:43.981 --> 08:44.941
[whimpers]

08:45.024 --> 08:45.983
[sniffs]

08:46.859 --> 08:48.569
I didn't want to lose.

08:50.071 --> 08:51.072
[sighs] What now?

08:51.864 --> 08:53.574
Should I just skip this life?

08:54.742 --> 08:56.702
Ka-young could live
up to 80 years at most.

08:58.287 --> 08:59.872
-[buttons clack]
-Those 80 years

08:59.956 --> 09:02.208
would slip by with this lamp
and those aluminum kettles.

09:02.291 --> 09:04.919
And the money to do that,
how will that work?

09:05.002 --> 09:07.213
Yeah, you're right.
Better to skip this life.

09:07.296 --> 09:09.465
So, for now, I'll just pass undetected.

09:10.299 --> 09:13.469
You need to get hired at her garage
so you can rummage for info. Okay?

09:13.553 --> 09:16.806
Oh, so you're just gonna live off me…

09:17.515 --> 09:19.267
Where can I find you, Master,
if I need you?

09:22.436 --> 09:24.730
I shall hide away above the ground.

09:25.606 --> 09:27.358
Somewhere close to Him.

09:27.984 --> 09:30.111
-[whooshing]
-[dramatic music playing]

09:34.657 --> 09:35.700
[door slides]

09:37.201 --> 09:39.996
-[Pan-geum] Come on. Time to eat.
-No, sorry. I'm in a hurry.

09:40.079 --> 09:41.330
Oh, wait.

09:41.414 --> 09:42.915
I know just where to eat that.

09:43.583 --> 09:45.543
If you don't mind,
don't tell Ka-young about this.

09:53.801 --> 09:55.261
[groans]

09:55.344 --> 09:57.388
[carpet whizzing]

10:01.100 --> 10:03.394
[jaunty music playing]

10:06.772 --> 10:07.648
[slurps]

10:08.232 --> 10:09.191
Mm!

10:10.318 --> 10:12.612
This is really scrumptious.

10:14.030 --> 10:15.448
[engines whirring]

10:17.033 --> 10:19.035
[daunting music plays]

10:21.203 --> 10:23.039
[man on radio] What's going on?
Status report.

10:23.122 --> 10:25.249
[pilot 1] Unidentified
flying object spotted.

10:25.333 --> 10:26.167
[chuckles]

10:26.876 --> 10:28.502
Is… Is that a carpet? Over.

10:29.754 --> 10:30.671
Whoa.

10:31.464 --> 10:33.549
[pilot 2] What the--
He's eating bibimbap! Over!

10:34.383 --> 10:37.261
[man] What are you talking about?
Give me a proper report!

10:42.391 --> 10:44.393
Hmm? What is it?

10:44.477 --> 10:45.895
What do you want?

10:45.978 --> 10:46.812
Huh?

10:48.648 --> 10:50.775
Oh! Are you two meeting each other?

10:51.359 --> 10:52.193
Gotcha!

10:52.276 --> 10:53.903
[pilot 2] He's fleeing! Awaiting orders.

10:53.986 --> 10:55.613
[pilot 1] Permission
to shoot down. Over.

10:55.696 --> 10:56.947
[announcer] At 3:39 p.m. today,

10:57.031 --> 10:59.909
the Ministry of National Defense
reported an unidentified flying object

10:59.992 --> 11:02.662
in the maritime border area
between South Korea and Japan,

11:02.745 --> 11:05.498
leading to a fighter jet standoff
between the two countries.

11:05.581 --> 11:08.834
They've avoided providing any details
regarding the flying object.

11:14.840 --> 11:17.051
[Ka-young] It seems
I've identified our flying object.

11:18.219 --> 11:19.387
With remarkable detail.

11:19.470 --> 11:21.806
I just took a little excursion
to think about it all.

11:23.349 --> 11:24.183
Little?

11:24.266 --> 11:27.520
Your little excursion
nearly caused a war to break out.

11:27.603 --> 11:30.106
You just had to take
to the skies to have your lunch.

11:30.189 --> 11:31.190
Bibimbap!

11:32.441 --> 11:34.610
I hear you're looking for help, Ms. Ki.

11:35.444 --> 11:37.029
[whispering] Stop.

11:38.197 --> 11:39.240
Just wait.

11:39.949 --> 11:40.825
[sighs]

11:40.908 --> 11:44.078
I'm a very good employee.
I'm passionate about cars.

11:44.161 --> 11:47.331
-They're my bread and butter.
-Oh, uh, why don't we…

11:47.415 --> 11:50.835
maybe not talk about food right now?

11:53.295 --> 11:54.713
What's going on?

11:55.339 --> 11:56.632
[suspenseful music plays]

11:56.715 --> 11:58.717
You two are clearly friends.

12:04.014 --> 12:06.183
I thought you said
you were gonna, you know,

12:06.267 --> 12:08.144
keep yourself out of sight from her.

12:08.227 --> 12:11.063
You blew your cover. I have an idea.

12:13.149 --> 12:14.400
I better change tactics.

12:15.234 --> 12:17.987
But what can you possibly do
under a bridge?

12:18.070 --> 12:22.324
Why did Ki Ka-young die for them
when she had no interest in dying for me?

12:23.075 --> 12:24.577
What about them versus me?

12:25.953 --> 12:27.163
I must find the answer.

12:28.539 --> 12:29.373
Wait here.

12:29.999 --> 12:31.834
Huh? Damn it.

12:31.917 --> 12:33.419
[shouts] Where are you going?

12:34.753 --> 12:36.755
[suspenseful music plays]

12:37.882 --> 12:41.677
Comrades. May we will meet again,
alive at Harbin Station.

12:42.761 --> 12:43.804
Yes.

12:48.184 --> 12:49.185
[Iblis] Ki Ka-young?

12:50.769 --> 12:51.770
Oh. [chuckles]

12:52.480 --> 12:53.314
Who are you?

12:53.397 --> 12:55.357
Pleased to meet you,
past-life Ka-young.

12:55.441 --> 12:56.525
One quick question.

12:58.569 --> 13:00.946
-Do you know an An Jung-geun?
-[running footsteps]

13:01.030 --> 13:03.407
Comrades! We've been compromised!

13:03.491 --> 13:05.534
Everybody run! Now! [panting]

13:07.036 --> 13:08.329
Been spying on us, have you?

13:08.412 --> 13:10.873
Spying? What's spying?

13:11.624 --> 13:14.126
-No, I just wanna ask you something.
-[running footsteps]

13:14.210 --> 13:15.961
[guns cocking]

13:16.045 --> 13:17.630
-[man 1] Fire!
-[man 2] Run!

13:17.713 --> 13:19.173
[gunshots]

13:19.256 --> 13:20.966
Ah, so loud. I don't like it.

13:24.720 --> 13:27.056
[groaning] Stop it! That hurts!

13:27.139 --> 13:29.308
Hey! We were in the middle of something.

13:29.391 --> 13:30.851
I don't want these things.

13:33.687 --> 13:35.940
[soldiers grunting and groaning]

13:38.901 --> 13:42.112
Oh, no. I was just trying to return
those things to you. Right, Ki Ka-young.

13:43.113 --> 13:45.366
Where are you going? Ki Ka-young! Hold up!

13:45.449 --> 13:47.826
I haven't asked you my question.
It'll only take a second.

13:48.494 --> 13:49.662
[panting]

13:49.745 --> 13:51.247
Thank you for saving me.

13:52.581 --> 13:54.708
If there's more life beyond this,

13:55.584 --> 13:57.127
I hope we meet again.

13:57.211 --> 13:59.547
Wait, no.
I wanna talk to you in this life.

14:00.089 --> 14:01.340
[man] Get that one! Him!

14:01.423 --> 14:02.675
-Fire!
-[gunshots]

14:02.758 --> 14:05.970
[groans] That stings, that stings!
I told you, I don't want these!

14:06.804 --> 14:07.930
[soldiers groaning]

14:08.013 --> 14:09.557
-Oh, Ki Ka-young.
-[man 2] Over there!

14:09.640 --> 14:11.809
-Don't let him get away!
-Oh. Wait…

14:11.892 --> 14:13.644
[sighs] This life won't do.

14:16.105 --> 14:18.440
-[man 3] Where'd he go?
-[man 2] Find him.

14:18.524 --> 14:20.734
THE YEAR 1592

14:20.818 --> 14:23.279
[dramatic music playing]

14:27.950 --> 14:29.618
[horse neighing]

14:30.244 --> 14:32.079
[Chang-sik] A messenger
from the naval command

14:32.162 --> 14:33.747
of the Jeolla province has arrived.

14:33.831 --> 14:34.832
[king] Let him in.

14:37.877 --> 14:39.169
Deliver your scroll.

14:40.087 --> 14:41.088
Yes, sir.

14:45.968 --> 14:47.011
[Iblis] Ki Ka-young.

14:54.810 --> 14:56.061
Ki Ka-young.

14:56.145 --> 14:59.023
-[man 1] Who's saying that?
-[man 2 whispers] Is someone's speaking?

14:59.106 --> 15:00.316
Oh, so you're a man?

15:01.525 --> 15:03.068
-[Ka-young gasps]
-[man] Whoa.

15:04.403 --> 15:05.529
-What's going on?
-Unusual.

15:06.155 --> 15:08.157
[men whispering]

15:10.242 --> 15:11.452
Ki Ka-young.

15:11.535 --> 15:13.037
I've gotta ask you a question.

15:13.120 --> 15:16.582
"Your Majesty. I, Yi Sun-sin,
General of the Jeolla Province,

15:16.665 --> 15:17.875
-offer this report…"
-Right.

15:17.958 --> 15:20.127
It's about that person there. Yi Sun-sin.

15:20.210 --> 15:22.212
"…the front line of the enemy forces
at Busan Port,

15:22.296 --> 15:23.756
and in doing so,
managed to sink…"

15:23.839 --> 15:25.591
-Ki Ka-young.
-"…100 Ki Ka-young--"

15:25.674 --> 15:28.844
[sighs] "One hu-Ki-- No, one hundred--"

15:28.928 --> 15:30.930
Sire, I willingly accept death
as punishment.

15:31.013 --> 15:32.514
-[king] Who was that?
-[Iblis] Mm.

15:32.598 --> 15:33.432
Show yourself.

15:34.350 --> 15:36.852
Who keeps going on
about this Ki Ka-young?

15:38.854 --> 15:39.730
[chuckles softly]

15:40.981 --> 15:41.941
[Iblis] Oh.

15:42.608 --> 15:45.235
-Uh…
-[man 1] What is this sorcery?

15:45.319 --> 15:48.530
-[man 2] Who is this?
-[man 3] Where did he come from?

15:48.614 --> 15:49.990
[man 2] Is he a person or a ghost?

15:50.074 --> 15:51.742
I just had an important question.

15:51.825 --> 15:53.035
[man 1] How did he sneak in?

15:53.619 --> 15:56.080
That-- That strange, tall, towering man…

15:56.747 --> 15:58.666
-Seize that necromancer!
-[man] Yes, sir.

15:58.749 --> 16:00.709
-Off with his head!
-[man] Yes. Yes, take him.

16:00.793 --> 16:01.710
Off?

16:02.461 --> 16:03.462
[man 2] Be gone with him.

16:03.545 --> 16:04.546
How does that work?

16:06.674 --> 16:09.259
[radio narrator]
One unofficial Joseon text stated

16:09.343 --> 16:13.722
that the being stayed alive
for three whole days after being beheaded.

16:13.806 --> 16:17.142
For all three days,
it continued its bizarre ranting,

16:17.226 --> 16:20.062
crying out, "Ki Ka-young, Ki Ka-young,"

16:20.145 --> 16:22.773
before suddenly disappearing
in a burst of dust.

16:25.693 --> 16:26.610
Where have you been?

16:27.236 --> 16:29.488
Far away. [chuckles wryly]

16:30.656 --> 16:31.615
[bones crunch]

16:31.699 --> 16:33.117
-[groans]
-[neck cracks]

16:36.203 --> 16:39.289
I… met up with an old friend
from long ago.

16:39.373 --> 16:40.749
[Iblis chuckles]

16:40.833 --> 16:43.419
You. What are you playing at?

16:43.502 --> 16:46.588
You wouldn't shut up about my wishes,
yet now that I've made one, you vanish.

16:47.256 --> 16:49.466
You're just putting off
your end of the deal!

16:50.050 --> 16:50.926
That's not it.

16:51.010 --> 16:53.095
It's all going according to my plans.

16:53.178 --> 16:55.639
They'll only see the lamp
when their desires peak.

16:58.225 --> 16:59.768
I wonder, how would I know

16:59.852 --> 17:02.187
if something in the world changed
because of their wishes?

17:02.271 --> 17:03.605
That arranged too?

17:09.194 --> 17:10.487
So you're saying there's a quill

17:10.571 --> 17:14.241
that ensures whatever is written
will forever last no matter what changes?

17:14.324 --> 17:16.994
The magic quill's here?
And we had to be here this early?

17:17.077 --> 17:18.912
[Iblis] Yes. It'll be right here.

17:18.996 --> 17:21.081
Truth is, the process is tricky.

17:22.666 --> 17:24.752
I'll be expecting your assistance.

17:24.835 --> 17:27.004
[door opens, closes]

17:29.590 --> 17:31.467
[suspenseful music plays]

17:32.634 --> 17:35.262
That man is the property owner.
He gave you permission to be here?

17:35.345 --> 17:38.557
Permission is not a word
that's in our vocabulary.

17:39.892 --> 17:41.852
So pull it quick when his guard's down.

17:42.644 --> 17:43.771
Then run.

17:45.731 --> 17:46.732
What?

17:47.566 --> 17:48.442
[gasps]

17:49.985 --> 17:50.944
Oh, you son of a…

17:51.820 --> 17:52.988
[laughing]

17:53.072 --> 17:54.698
[Ka-young screaming]

17:54.782 --> 17:56.575
-[man shouting]
-[Ka-young] This is fun!

17:56.658 --> 17:58.827
-[man screaming]
-[Ka-young laughing]

17:58.911 --> 18:00.329
[man] I've got you. [gasping]

18:00.412 --> 18:02.081
[man screaming]

18:04.166 --> 18:05.834
[man whimpers]

18:05.918 --> 18:07.336
[man screams]

18:09.004 --> 18:11.006
[both screaming]

18:13.092 --> 18:14.802
[man panting]

18:17.638 --> 18:18.889
Are you okay?

18:18.972 --> 18:20.265
Yes, I'm all right.

18:21.433 --> 18:24.228
Uh, why were you screaming,
when you have wings?

18:24.812 --> 18:26.438
I haven't flown in a while, that's all.

18:27.231 --> 18:28.607
Your garage doing well?

18:28.690 --> 18:30.192
Suppose you could say that.

18:31.443 --> 18:33.654
I'm sorry, this might sting a little.

18:34.696 --> 18:35.614
[groans]

18:36.490 --> 18:38.742
Oh, come on,
I'm molting enough as it is.

18:39.535 --> 18:41.703
Hey! How many did you pluck off?

18:41.787 --> 18:43.330
[sighing]

18:44.081 --> 18:45.958
[Iblis] It's been a while, brother.

18:47.084 --> 18:49.294
Those thousand years just flew by.

18:49.378 --> 18:50.838
Nice to see you, brother.

18:51.755 --> 18:55.092
So, peace reigned on Earth
during my absence, I guess?

18:55.759 --> 18:57.553
You claimed humans
were only ever corrupted

18:57.636 --> 18:59.429
because I lure them to it. [laughs]

18:59.513 --> 19:03.183
So I have to imagine there were only good
humans in the world when I was imprisoned.

19:03.267 --> 19:07.312
Strange that war, greed, arrogance
and selfishness continued to exist,

19:08.021 --> 19:09.148
even when I was gone.

19:09.231 --> 19:12.025
Consider the power of the seeds
you dutifully planted.

19:12.109 --> 19:15.571
Do you not think that even offering
humans wishes is wrong in itself?

19:16.446 --> 19:18.407
-I'm not sure you do.
-You know like I do.

19:19.074 --> 19:22.452
These half-finished lumps of clay
were a mistake of His.

19:22.536 --> 19:25.164
It is he who has charged me
with proving this,

19:25.831 --> 19:27.791
that Hell is their only recourse.

19:27.875 --> 19:30.794
Don't forget that
He assigned a task to me as well.

19:30.878 --> 19:34.089
Did you not also steal a feather from me
before you were detained?

19:34.173 --> 19:35.674
What plot are you fermenting now?

19:35.757 --> 19:37.551
[laughs] Oh!

19:37.634 --> 19:38.927
You think I'll tell you?

19:39.595 --> 19:42.306
I know that every day of my imprisonment,
no matter what,

19:43.307 --> 19:45.726
you came to visit
the desert where I was buried.

19:45.809 --> 19:49.521
And every day, you added
a handful of sand on top.

19:49.605 --> 19:50.689
Heavy, was it?

19:50.772 --> 19:54.151
You should try experiencing
the weight of life that humans feel.

19:54.234 --> 19:57.696
[laughs] My goodness.
Talk about a true angel.

20:00.115 --> 20:02.075
We do need to catch up properly.

20:02.784 --> 20:05.287
If you'd like.
Though I must advise we do it soon.

20:06.955 --> 20:09.208
Because I'll be coming
for your throat next.

20:09.875 --> 20:11.793
-[gasps jokingly]
-[exhales derisively]

20:18.133 --> 20:19.426
[laughs]

20:19.509 --> 20:21.178
[panting]

20:23.055 --> 20:24.431
What? Where did he go?

20:41.281 --> 20:43.283
[upbeat soul music playing]

20:51.833 --> 20:53.502
-[muffled thudding]
-[gasps]

20:54.711 --> 20:57.047
Hey! Oh, come on! Damn it!

20:57.130 --> 20:58.382
You, you, you, you, you--

20:59.716 --> 21:01.927
My building. You flew right through it.

21:02.010 --> 21:03.845
You crazy? All the units are sold.

21:03.929 --> 21:05.514
They'll start moving in on Monday,

21:05.597 --> 21:06.723
-you ass!
-[laughing]

21:06.807 --> 21:08.809
Do you even know
the market value of this building?

21:08.892 --> 21:10.102
Let's see.

21:10.185 --> 21:12.980
Is it the price of your hypocrisy?

21:13.063 --> 21:14.898
-Why, you little!
-[laughing]

21:14.982 --> 21:18.694
Wow. For a minute,
I forgot your name is literally Satan.

21:18.777 --> 21:20.487
I take it you remember now?

21:22.572 --> 21:23.949
Watch your back, Su-hyeon.

21:25.117 --> 21:27.286
I have returned. Get ready.

21:29.037 --> 21:29.997
[laughs]

21:31.540 --> 21:32.958
You, you, you, damn it!

21:34.084 --> 21:35.127
[sighs]

21:35.210 --> 21:36.962
[grunting in frustration]

21:52.436 --> 21:54.646
So this quill will only write the truth?

22:00.986 --> 22:04.489
WRITTEN BY KI KA-YOUNG

22:04.573 --> 22:08.744
A NEGATIVE ONE AND STONE IN A SHOE.

22:15.292 --> 22:19.212
THE GENIE HAS GOOD LOOKS.

22:20.839 --> 22:21.757
It works.

22:22.799 --> 22:24.051
THE GENIE HAS LOOKS.

22:24.718 --> 22:26.803
Well, that's harsh but fair.

22:32.601 --> 22:34.436
I AM…

22:37.647 --> 22:40.400
I AM GRANDMA'S BURDEN.

22:43.945 --> 22:45.697
I AM GRANDMA'S STRENGTH.

22:49.534 --> 22:51.536
[pensive music playing]

22:54.581 --> 22:57.375
Ka-young. Try some of these.

22:58.043 --> 23:00.337
Chang-sik gave us a ton of them.

23:00.420 --> 23:01.630
They're very sweet.

23:04.841 --> 23:06.510
-Grandma.
-What?

23:08.261 --> 23:10.722
For so long, I've believed a lie.

23:10.806 --> 23:12.974
I'm not a burden on you,
I'm your strength.

23:13.975 --> 23:14.810
Grandma!

23:14.893 --> 23:18.396
Ka-young, you're only realizing that now?

23:18.480 --> 23:22.442
You may've been top of your class,
but clearly you're not so clever. [laughs]

23:22.526 --> 23:24.736
Eat up, so you can be strong too.

23:24.820 --> 23:26.905
[laughs, sighs]

23:26.988 --> 23:31.159
Grandma, strawberries contain vitamin C,
not strength.

23:31.910 --> 23:35.789
For strength, you should consume
a primary energy source, like carbs.

23:35.872 --> 23:36.873
Grandma?

23:37.541 --> 23:39.543
[dreamy music playing]

23:44.131 --> 23:46.341
[groaning]

23:49.427 --> 23:52.180
What are you sitting here
daydreaming about?

23:52.264 --> 23:53.932
Gonna do any work?

23:54.766 --> 23:56.935
-Gonna sell these strawberries next year?
-[shouts]

23:57.519 --> 23:58.395
I'm not thinking.

23:59.271 --> 24:00.272
It was one-sided.

24:01.773 --> 24:02.774
It wasn't mutual.

24:03.441 --> 24:04.276
Oh, by the way,

24:04.359 --> 24:08.071
I heard that greeting by rubbing noses
is common in the Middle East.

24:08.155 --> 24:11.950
They do it if they have the utmost respect
for you, like dignitaries.

24:12.033 --> 24:14.619
-What? So, I'm a dignitary?
-Sure.

24:14.703 --> 24:16.371
[chuckles in disbelief]

24:16.454 --> 24:17.414
[groans]

24:17.497 --> 24:19.499
[laughing]

24:23.879 --> 24:25.797
-You are my darling, love!
-Yeah.

24:25.881 --> 24:28.300
Peace has returned
to our very briefly shaken-up family.

24:28.383 --> 24:30.510
[woman] All right. All right. [groans]

24:30.594 --> 24:31.970
-[squealing softly]
-Okay, enough.

24:32.053 --> 24:33.763
What kind of bullshit is all this?

24:33.847 --> 24:35.223
Come on, get back to work.

24:35.307 --> 24:37.434
Didn't you say there's a raffle
for the festival too?

24:37.517 --> 24:39.477
-Enough!
-[gasps, shouts]

24:40.145 --> 24:41.688
I need everyone on their top game

24:41.771 --> 24:44.232
to ensure sales do not drop
during the festival.

24:44.316 --> 24:45.942
Corporate is strict about it.

24:46.026 --> 24:48.236
It's crucial that the displays
are neat and full,

24:48.320 --> 24:49.988
and don't forget to offer more samples.

24:50.071 --> 24:51.281
[staff] Yes, ma'am.

24:51.364 --> 24:52.407
[sighs] Kang Im-seon.

24:52.490 --> 24:56.244
How many times have I told you
to put some effort into your appearance?

24:56.328 --> 24:58.330
Remove that patch too.

25:01.208 --> 25:02.083
Well?

25:02.167 --> 25:03.210
You even listening?

25:03.293 --> 25:05.795
Yes, Assistant Branch Manager Lee.

25:11.051 --> 25:12.219
[groans]

25:21.978 --> 25:22.896
[Im-seon] Huh?

25:23.605 --> 25:24.481
What's this?

25:26.358 --> 25:28.151
When did we start selling these?

25:30.278 --> 25:31.488
[blows]

25:31.571 --> 25:32.530
Wow, really?

25:32.614 --> 25:33.865
Come on.

25:36.034 --> 25:38.036
[magical music playing]

25:50.257 --> 25:51.258
[soft boom]

25:51.341 --> 25:52.384
[yelps]

25:54.052 --> 25:55.387
[whimpering]

25:58.515 --> 25:59.474
What the…

26:00.475 --> 26:02.852
You have awoken the spirit of the lamp.

26:03.979 --> 26:05.855
I shall grant you three wishes.

26:05.939 --> 26:07.524
[gasping]

26:08.817 --> 26:09.818
Make them.

26:11.778 --> 26:13.571
No bringing back the dead.

26:14.364 --> 26:15.573
Or travel to the future.

26:16.408 --> 26:18.743
But anything other than that,

26:18.827 --> 26:20.620
your wish…

26:22.205 --> 26:23.456
is my command.

26:25.709 --> 26:27.711
[Im-seon breathing shakily]

26:28.962 --> 26:30.672
[music building]

26:33.091 --> 26:34.592
She made her first wish?

26:37.053 --> 26:38.305
[Iblis] Hmm.

26:38.388 --> 26:40.098
I understand the negative one.

26:41.266 --> 26:43.226
But what's up with the stone thing?

26:44.102 --> 26:45.395
There always something with you.

26:45.478 --> 26:46.479
None of your business.

26:47.522 --> 26:49.774
Tell me, what did Ms. Kang wish for?

26:51.526 --> 26:52.444
[scoffs]

26:55.739 --> 27:00.910
KANG IM-SEON, SUPERMARKET EMPLOYEE

27:07.834 --> 27:09.044
Good morning, all.

27:09.127 --> 27:11.880
My name is Kang Im-seon,
and I'm your manager.

27:15.759 --> 27:18.470
I've been working
at this supermarket for 20 years,

27:19.179 --> 27:20.638
ever since it opened.

27:21.306 --> 27:24.434
[breath trembling] That young bitch
gets to be assistant branch manager

27:24.517 --> 27:25.769
just because she has a degree?

27:26.728 --> 27:28.229
I don't even get good hours.

27:29.147 --> 27:30.106
[gasps]

27:30.774 --> 27:33.318
I wish to be
that lady's superior officer here.

27:33.902 --> 27:35.111
The store manager.

27:37.489 --> 27:38.990
That's my first wish.

27:39.074 --> 27:41.368
[dramatic music playing]

27:42.952 --> 27:44.871
-[indistinct chatter]
-[man] Is she for real?

27:44.954 --> 27:47.665
My goodness, Im-seon. Congratulations.

27:48.416 --> 27:50.293
She's been working so hard.

27:50.377 --> 27:51.252
Well deserved.

27:54.464 --> 27:56.633
Assistant Branch Manager Lee?

27:56.716 --> 27:59.010
You will display
the special frozen goods today.

27:59.094 --> 28:00.387
-What?
-[chuckles dryly]

28:00.470 --> 28:02.764
Well, you were never satisfied
with their layout.

28:03.431 --> 28:05.350
And wear a lighter shade of lipstick.

28:05.433 --> 28:08.603
Tone down the perfume
before you walk around the sample areas.

28:09.729 --> 28:11.231
You have something to say?

28:11.898 --> 28:13.149
[snaps fingers]

28:13.233 --> 28:14.234
You even listening?

28:16.444 --> 28:18.405
Yes. Yes, ma'am.

28:20.490 --> 28:21.324
[Im-seon] Hmm.

28:21.908 --> 28:24.744
Perk up. Let's open the doors.

28:24.828 --> 28:25.870
[staff] Yes, ma'am.

28:27.622 --> 28:29.374
What in the world just happened?

28:30.375 --> 28:34.295
I know! How does one lowly restocker
become our boss just like that?

28:34.379 --> 28:35.380
What is going on?

28:35.463 --> 28:36.923
[woman] Who knows?

28:38.341 --> 28:39.634
[Im-seon] Ah.

28:39.717 --> 28:41.052
You're due for an oil change.

28:41.845 --> 28:43.388
Oh, yeah.

28:44.806 --> 28:47.642
Actually, I'm buying a new car.

28:48.476 --> 28:49.477
A foreign one.

28:50.103 --> 28:51.688
So, you don't have to worry.

28:56.735 --> 28:58.737
Are you seeing it now?

28:58.820 --> 29:00.530
How easily you're corrupted?

29:01.281 --> 29:03.700
There's one thing
I definitely didn't think of.

29:03.783 --> 29:05.410
Didn't know I'd lose a client.

29:06.327 --> 29:09.497
Wait. Why are you
showing yourself like this?

29:09.581 --> 29:11.458
She's already seen you as a Genie.

29:11.541 --> 29:14.002
-Shouldn't you be staying out of sight?
-[scoffs]

29:14.753 --> 29:17.213
In their eyes, I am but a tiny dust bunny.

29:18.006 --> 29:21.426
But I do radiate a glow
to appear more magical.

29:21.509 --> 29:24.220
That's it in a nutshell. [chuckles]

29:26.431 --> 29:29.184
Min-ji wears a white robe at her clinic
to seem more like a doctor.

29:29.267 --> 29:30.310
Oh!

29:30.393 --> 29:33.229
If she were to hold a syringe
without the robe on…

29:34.439 --> 29:35.482
Hmm.

29:37.609 --> 29:39.569
That's where you're cutting it off?

29:39.652 --> 29:41.696
Wow. That's cruel.

29:44.616 --> 29:47.702
Hey, so who even is this Min-ji?
I've been dying to know.

29:49.913 --> 29:52.207
[girl 1] Move your head out of the way,
Choi Min-ji.

29:52.290 --> 29:54.793
You're blocking
Lil Miss Psychopath's head.

29:58.046 --> 30:01.716
Hey! Is it true you think
about murdering people and stuff?

30:01.800 --> 30:03.301
Like chopping them up?

30:05.970 --> 30:07.096
I just did.

30:07.722 --> 30:09.557
-You just did?
-[girls laughing]

30:09.641 --> 30:11.226
Oh, that's fucked up. [laughs]

30:11.309 --> 30:12.811
Stop pulling her hair.

30:12.894 --> 30:15.897
She might not admit that it hurts,
but it's still painful.

30:15.980 --> 30:17.857
That's the idea, weirdo. [laughs]

30:17.941 --> 30:21.861
That's why we pull her hair.
'Cause it's painful. [chuckles]

30:24.239 --> 30:26.658
[young Ka-young] You do it
even though you know it hurts her?

30:27.242 --> 30:30.453
You know the rules,
and still you go and break 'em?

30:30.537 --> 30:31.913
[suspenseful music plays]

30:31.996 --> 30:33.456
[girls chuckling]

30:34.833 --> 30:36.125
[girl 1] Fuck, this is boring.

30:36.751 --> 30:38.837
Let's just finish this cigarette
and get out of here.

30:42.215 --> 30:44.050
[watch ticking]

30:46.719 --> 30:47.554
[stall door opens]

30:49.556 --> 30:52.559
Ugh, what's that smell?
Is that gasoline?

30:52.642 --> 30:54.352
Ugh, that gas stench.

30:54.435 --> 30:56.729
This weirdo again.
What the fuck are you doing?

30:56.813 --> 30:58.022
Setting the place on fire.

30:58.690 --> 31:00.900
You were smoking,
so clearly you guys started it.

31:00.984 --> 31:03.361
Ah, do we look like dipshits,
you psycho bitch?

31:03.444 --> 31:05.488
-You see all these witnesses?
-[girls screaming]

31:05.572 --> 31:06.948
-Shit!
-[girl 2] Fuck.

31:07.031 --> 31:07.949
And now?

31:08.575 --> 31:10.743
Shall I eliminate the witnesses, then?

31:10.827 --> 31:12.912
-[lighter clicks]
-[girl 1] Okay, okay, we get it.

31:12.996 --> 31:14.956
All right.
Okay, we'll do whatever you want.

31:15.039 --> 31:16.541
Don't mess with Choi Min-ji.

31:17.333 --> 31:18.543
This is our new rule.

31:18.626 --> 31:20.420
[breathing heavily] All right.

31:22.046 --> 31:23.047
[lighter snaps shut]

31:26.050 --> 31:29.178
Be my friend.
Neither of us have any other friend.

31:30.221 --> 31:33.224
It's more efficient to be a duo
than alone in South Korea.

31:34.225 --> 31:36.102
And what if I don't
wanna be friends with you?

31:36.185 --> 31:37.604
You have no other option.

31:37.687 --> 31:39.439
So, we are friends from now on.

31:41.524 --> 31:43.401
Also, you're terrible at school.

31:43.484 --> 31:46.112
Memorize all of this.
I'll murder you if you don't.

31:46.905 --> 31:47.739
MATH I

31:47.822 --> 31:49.949
Complete these.
I'll murder you if you don't.

31:50.033 --> 31:51.117
[sighs]

31:53.077 --> 31:56.122
Make sure you pass the oral exam.
I'll murder you if you don't.

31:56.205 --> 31:57.832
Honestly, it's a helpful motivator.

31:58.625 --> 32:00.084
There's no other option.

32:00.877 --> 32:02.128
Pass, Choi Min-ji!

32:04.422 --> 32:07.592
How funny.
It says, "Weirdos especially welcome."

32:07.675 --> 32:09.677
-How absurd.
-So strange.

32:09.761 --> 32:14.057
My experience has taught me
that weirdos can change the world.

32:14.140 --> 32:17.018
[woman] One of the people
chosen for Ms. Ki Ka-young's first wish

32:17.101 --> 32:18.853
has in turn made their first wish.

32:18.937 --> 32:21.898
Cheongpung has altered
from the reality of yesterday.

32:21.981 --> 32:23.733
[squeals] Well done, Master.

32:24.776 --> 32:27.779
As long as we steer
Ms. Ki's remaining wishes to plan,

32:27.862 --> 32:30.990
you will be on track to do
what you have so long prepared for.

32:31.074 --> 32:32.784
Slitting that evil Iblis's throat.

32:32.867 --> 32:35.411
That's why they wanted my feather.
A record.

32:36.537 --> 32:37.455
Hmm.

32:37.538 --> 32:40.833
But you know, I've been studying
psychopaths for 20 years.

32:41.417 --> 32:44.420
I thought Ki Ka-young
would never make any wish.

32:44.504 --> 32:46.923
Still, I'm glad for this stroke of luck.

32:47.006 --> 32:48.383
But something feels off.

32:49.676 --> 32:52.929
Psychopaths are tricky.
I might need to read up on her kind again.

32:53.638 --> 32:55.056
Back to business.

32:55.139 --> 32:57.558
-What's Iblis doing?
-Gaming and chugging beer.

32:59.727 --> 33:01.729
-He'll come when he's low on funds.
-Yes.

33:02.397 --> 33:04.816
-He's mooching off Sade for now.
-Why, that…

33:04.899 --> 33:07.652
And someone has been trolling
our website since yesterday.

33:08.277 --> 33:10.989
Looking at the content and typos,
it seems quite clear…

33:11.656 --> 33:12.949
the culprit is Iblis.

33:14.575 --> 33:15.410
That son of a…

33:16.035 --> 33:17.954
[grunting]

33:22.166 --> 33:24.794
[grunting and groaning]

33:24.877 --> 33:26.045
Oh.

33:27.630 --> 33:28.798
Oh, no. No, no, no.

33:29.549 --> 33:31.009
Come on. No.

33:31.092 --> 33:32.719
[objects rattling]

33:33.469 --> 33:35.722
Hang on, Sang-hyeok did this
and found money.

33:40.143 --> 33:41.519
[game announcer] Game over!

33:46.899 --> 33:48.067
Hey, human.

33:51.612 --> 33:53.322
Who? Me?

33:57.660 --> 33:59.120
What do you want?

33:59.203 --> 34:01.873
Pick that up. The Earth is in pain.

34:01.956 --> 34:04.667
Even Ka-young doesn't litter.
What makes you feel you can?

34:04.751 --> 34:06.586
-[chuckles]
-In pain?

34:07.503 --> 34:09.797
Ah, the poor Earth.

34:09.881 --> 34:12.091
Ah, what a truly generous person you are.

34:18.681 --> 34:19.807
[exhales loudly]

34:19.891 --> 34:22.351
I think I'll toss this one too.
That make you mad?

34:22.435 --> 34:23.561
What're you gonna do?

34:23.644 --> 34:24.645
Wow.

34:25.813 --> 34:26.898
Just my kind of guy.

34:26.981 --> 34:28.441
[exhales loudly]

34:29.150 --> 34:31.277
We'd be friends on any other day.

34:31.944 --> 34:33.112
Today is the exception.

34:33.196 --> 34:35.156
Sade!

34:35.823 --> 34:37.742
[whooshing]

34:40.286 --> 34:41.412
-[man gasps]
-Yes, Master.

34:41.496 --> 34:43.456
What kind of magic trick is this?

34:44.082 --> 34:45.208
How'd you run so fast?

34:45.291 --> 34:46.709
Deal with that lump of clay.

34:46.793 --> 34:48.878
And give me any change you've got.

34:50.379 --> 34:52.048
[coins jingling]

34:52.131 --> 34:54.550
[man] Not gonna lie,
that was smooth.

34:55.593 --> 34:57.595
Stop staring at me
or I'll take your eyes out.

34:58.930 --> 35:00.014
[man scoffs]

35:00.807 --> 35:03.017
[tense music playing]

35:03.101 --> 35:04.352
Go for it. Come on.

35:04.435 --> 35:07.688
But I'm warning you. Touch me
and I'll sue your pathetic ass. Got it?

35:08.940 --> 35:10.066
[grunts]

35:10.858 --> 35:12.193
-[growls]
-[man screams]

35:12.276 --> 35:14.278
No!

35:14.362 --> 35:17.240
[crying and whimpering]

35:18.032 --> 35:19.992
-Get away! Help!
-[growling]

35:20.076 --> 35:20.952
[roars]

35:21.702 --> 35:24.163
[Sade growling]

35:25.456 --> 35:26.374
[owl hoots]

35:26.457 --> 35:27.458
[woman] Nice going.

35:27.542 --> 35:28.918
[Sade] Irem!

35:29.001 --> 35:30.044
[Irem hoots]

35:30.128 --> 35:33.214
[Sade] Has it been, what, 100 years?

35:34.298 --> 35:37.093
Oh, excuse me.
Have you seen a lady who looks like this?

35:37.760 --> 35:39.762
-[chuckles softly]
-[Irem hooting]

35:40.596 --> 35:42.932
Oh? [chuckles]

35:43.015 --> 35:45.768
-[Irem hoots]
-Irem!

35:45.852 --> 35:50.606
Have you been here
the whole time, since then?

35:50.690 --> 35:53.526
[Irem] Yes.
Ejllael decided to settle here.

35:53.609 --> 35:55.653
There were a lot of deaths back then.

35:55.736 --> 35:57.238
[wings fluttering]

35:57.321 --> 35:59.490
[Jong-heon] They said it was black,
so keep an eye out.

35:59.574 --> 36:00.867
[Chang-sik] Right, right. Black.

36:00.950 --> 36:03.035
[Min-jae] Wait, why are we
searching at night, then?

36:06.247 --> 36:08.583
Goddammit! What's that? Who's there?

36:08.666 --> 36:11.419
That's Ms. Irem, Director Ryu's assistant.
And Mr. Seo I-deuk!

36:11.502 --> 36:13.671
Now's not the time
for a secret nighttime date.

36:13.754 --> 36:17.300
A cougar or a panther has broken loose
and everyone's on high alert.

36:17.383 --> 36:19.677
Oh, isn't it a jaguar? I heard jaguar--

36:19.760 --> 36:21.262
-Mm?
-A jaguar?

36:21.345 --> 36:24.599
Look, whatever it is, it's hiding out
here. So let's all go back down right now.

36:24.682 --> 36:26.726
-It's too dangerous to stay.
-Yeah, sure. Good work.

36:26.809 --> 36:28.603
Hurry. Let's go. Let's go.

36:28.686 --> 36:30.021
-[Irem chuckles]
-Come on.

36:31.189 --> 36:32.440
Hold on.

36:32.523 --> 36:34.150
[suspenseful music plays]

36:34.233 --> 36:35.443
That tail…

36:37.653 --> 36:38.487
And those ears…

36:40.072 --> 36:41.073
[Sade sighs]

36:42.325 --> 36:43.951
Irem and I went to the zoo.

36:44.035 --> 36:45.244
They were in the gift shop.

36:45.328 --> 36:46.787
Pretty cute, don't you think?

36:46.871 --> 36:48.998
-[laughter]
-Is that so?

36:49.081 --> 36:50.541
They look so real. Okay, go home.

36:50.625 --> 36:52.126
-Get going. Hurry up.
-[chuckles]

36:52.210 --> 36:53.419
[heavy footsteps]

36:53.502 --> 36:55.087
[mice squeaking]

36:55.171 --> 36:57.715
-[Sade] So, are you ready…
-[yelps]

36:58.382 --> 37:00.343
…to fess up what you know about her?

37:00.426 --> 37:02.094
[brown mouse squeaking]

37:03.429 --> 37:04.847
-[chuckles]
-[brown mouse yelps]

37:04.931 --> 37:07.767
Don't let this Jaguar lose face. [growls]

37:07.850 --> 37:08.684
I'm hungry.

37:08.768 --> 37:10.853
[white mouse squeaking]

37:12.730 --> 37:14.148
Then…

37:14.232 --> 37:16.234
tell me what you saw last night.

37:17.026 --> 37:18.110
You can leave. Go on.

37:18.194 --> 37:20.279
[squeaking nervously]

37:20.363 --> 37:21.614
[chuckles menacingly]

37:22.531 --> 37:24.283
Still wanna die honorably?

37:24.367 --> 37:27.453
-[squeaking nervously]
-[Sade hisses, growls playfully]

37:27.536 --> 37:29.163
[gulping]

37:29.247 --> 37:32.041
So I did some digging
like you ordered me to.

37:32.124 --> 37:36.003
The garage is actually her side hustle.
She has another job.

37:36.087 --> 37:36.963
[keyboard clacks]

37:38.297 --> 37:39.632
[Ka-young sighs]

37:39.715 --> 37:41.008
Elon Musk.

37:41.092 --> 37:42.635
Does he deserve to live?

37:42.718 --> 37:44.136
[slams]

37:44.220 --> 37:46.222
[upbeat music playing]

37:51.435 --> 37:53.145
[groans]

37:53.229 --> 37:56.315
She must've amassed a lot of money.
Didn't care about her pen.

37:56.899 --> 38:00.194
And now, here comes the really big news.

38:00.278 --> 38:01.570
[Iblis] Hmm.

38:02.196 --> 38:04.407
Hey, why are you closed every day
with a four in it?

38:04.490 --> 38:07.118
Some superstition
around the number, Ms. Ki?

38:08.995 --> 38:10.246
Four signals death.

38:11.455 --> 38:13.249
Mm? Forces of death?

38:13.332 --> 38:15.710
Uh, no, that's not what I meant.

38:15.793 --> 38:17.670
Even in rain or snow, she makes sure

38:17.753 --> 38:19.922
-she sticks to her routine.
-Hmm.

38:20.006 --> 38:21.841
On the 4th, it's scuba diving.

38:21.924 --> 38:24.010
The 14th, it's hiking.
The 24th, woodworking.

38:24.093 --> 38:25.720
-And Wednesdays--
-Gamja-tang!

38:25.803 --> 38:27.430
Ah, you got it.

38:27.513 --> 38:28.931
[gasps]

38:30.641 --> 38:32.768
So that's what it's all for.

38:32.852 --> 38:34.937
[somber music plays]

38:46.657 --> 38:49.327
Making it seem as much
like an accident as possible.

38:50.244 --> 38:52.747
An equipment malfunction in the deep sea.

38:52.830 --> 38:55.541
[breathing heavily]

38:55.624 --> 38:57.877
Or stumble off a cliff while climbing.

38:57.960 --> 38:59.003
Whoa.

39:00.963 --> 39:02.048
[sighs]

39:02.131 --> 39:03.924
[machine whirring]

39:09.638 --> 39:10.765
[Iblis] This entire routine

39:11.766 --> 39:14.477
is Ki Ka-young's way
of preparing for her death.

39:15.394 --> 39:19.690
The human body is 70% water
and blood is the heaviest part.

39:20.358 --> 39:23.402
So thinking about it,
if you drain the body…

39:24.320 --> 39:29.075
then cut here, and here, here, and here…

39:30.159 --> 39:34.038
If you chop there, then stack the pieces,
then your coffin…

39:36.290 --> 39:38.209
would just need to be that size.

39:38.292 --> 39:41.003
Ms. Ki Ka-young.
I will be moving abroad soon.

39:42.088 --> 39:43.631
Business that bad?

39:52.556 --> 39:54.850
So she just bought the place.

39:56.560 --> 39:57.728
[sighs]

40:01.148 --> 40:02.149
Wow.

40:02.900 --> 40:03.734
A coffin too?

40:04.777 --> 40:05.611
[Iblis sighs]

40:05.694 --> 40:08.322
Once her grandmother passes,
she's doing it.

40:08.406 --> 40:11.909
And if she dies too early,
can't get revenge if she's already dead.

40:11.992 --> 40:13.411
Yes, we must prevent that.

40:14.662 --> 40:15.996
I have an idea.

40:17.206 --> 40:21.043
Oh Pan-geum must live as long as she can.

40:24.463 --> 40:27.007
Oh, God. Oh, God.
Oh, my back. [sighs]

40:27.091 --> 40:28.217
Good Lord.

40:29.510 --> 40:32.138
What the hell's the point in being so old?

40:32.721 --> 40:33.556
-No!
-What the--?

40:33.639 --> 40:34.598
What hurts?

40:35.766 --> 40:37.977
-Which part of your back? Face down.
-My God!

40:38.060 --> 40:40.229
-Here? Or here? How about here?
-Oh, my goodness.

40:40.312 --> 40:41.522
-What is happening?
-This part?

40:41.605 --> 40:43.649
How's that? Much better?
Don't you feel young again?

40:46.360 --> 40:48.362
[groaning]

40:48.988 --> 40:52.491
I'm wasting time crushing all this garlic,
might as well give up.

40:52.575 --> 40:54.493
-At my age…
-[Iblis] No!

40:54.577 --> 40:55.744
The garlic, hand it over.

40:56.370 --> 40:58.247
Do I grind it? Give it here.

40:58.998 --> 41:00.583
[crushing and grinding rapidly]

41:02.168 --> 41:05.963
So, you must really like Ka-young
if you moved from Dubai

41:06.046 --> 41:08.007
just to be with her, wouldn't you say?

41:08.090 --> 41:10.342
Well, I just knew the minute I saw her.

41:10.426 --> 41:12.803
Ki Ka-young was just the girl
I was waiting for.

41:12.887 --> 41:13.762
Oh, my.

41:14.555 --> 41:17.266
You knew just like that? Immediately?

41:17.349 --> 41:19.810
Well, at first,
Ka-young didn't believe it at all.

41:21.896 --> 41:24.356
So I took her to the top of a skyscraper.

41:24.440 --> 41:28.736
You mean that big one where you can see
for miles and miles under the stars?

41:28.819 --> 41:32.281
So, what did the two of you get up to
all the way up there?

41:32.364 --> 41:35.367
[inhales] That's not really suitable
for your ears.

41:36.368 --> 41:37.786
But I'll tell you this.

41:37.870 --> 41:40.748
Ki Ka-young is different
from all the women I've ever met.

41:40.831 --> 41:42.291
She drives me crazy.

41:42.374 --> 41:43.709
So I just grabbed her neck and--

41:43.792 --> 41:46.712
God! Stop that right now.
I can't listen to this.

41:46.795 --> 41:48.172
[Iblis chuckles]

41:48.255 --> 41:52.384
The important thing is,
the stars aligned for you, and pow!

41:52.468 --> 41:53.636
You two fell hard, huh?

41:53.719 --> 41:54.762
"Pow"?

41:56.222 --> 41:58.140
That wasn't quite the sound. Hmm.

41:58.224 --> 41:59.725
More of a loud thud.

41:59.808 --> 42:00.726
[chuckles]

42:00.809 --> 42:02.019
It makes me cry still.

42:03.062 --> 42:05.022
[crushing garlic]

42:05.105 --> 42:06.607
What are your four pillars?

42:06.690 --> 42:07.858
Uh, "four pillars"?

42:07.942 --> 42:12.112
Oh, the day you were born.
Do you know the time as well?

42:13.405 --> 42:15.074
Well, let's see.

42:15.157 --> 42:17.451
I was born on Thursday.

42:18.160 --> 42:22.706
13.8 billion years… ago.

42:22.790 --> 42:24.708
[amusing music plays]

42:27.503 --> 42:30.381
[smacks lips] I got a baby face.

42:34.677 --> 42:36.512
Oh, my, the field.

42:36.595 --> 42:39.431
I really should pull
those invasive weeds out.

42:40.140 --> 42:42.101
[amusing music plays]

42:42.184 --> 42:43.936
[grunting]

42:47.481 --> 42:49.275
[sickle whizzing]

42:49.358 --> 42:51.360
[continues grunting]

42:55.281 --> 42:56.115
[pants]

42:58.909 --> 43:02.454
Well, Pan-geum gets a long life while
Master's life is shortened drastically.

43:02.538 --> 43:04.290
-[panting]
-Here, I brought you a snack.

43:04.373 --> 43:07.084
There's something else I need to tell you.

43:07.167 --> 43:11.630
My employer asked
if she and I met in the past too.

43:11.714 --> 43:13.424
[panting]

43:15.134 --> 43:16.260
Meaning what?

43:17.052 --> 43:19.555
Of course. We met yesterday,
so we have met in the past.

43:19.638 --> 43:21.432
No, no. I mean in a previous life.

43:21.515 --> 43:22.516
[gasps]

43:23.934 --> 43:26.145
-Do you recall that time now?
-No.

43:26.228 --> 43:28.939
Your Genie friend said
we met 983 years ago,

43:29.023 --> 43:30.649
so did you and I meet too?

43:30.733 --> 43:32.276
Well, actually, we did.

43:32.359 --> 43:34.069
But why is it so important to you?

43:34.778 --> 43:36.447
I just wanna know
what happened back then.

43:38.866 --> 43:40.159
All those years ago.

43:41.952 --> 43:43.078
How did I die then?

43:43.162 --> 43:44.204
[sighs]

43:44.955 --> 43:47.041
She doesn't care about that life.

43:47.124 --> 43:48.876
She only cares about her death.

43:49.752 --> 43:51.337
I was imprisoned.

43:52.129 --> 43:56.050
[choking up]
983 years, thinking only of…

43:56.133 --> 43:57.968
[Iblis sniffles]

43:58.636 --> 43:59.928
Thinking of what?

44:00.012 --> 44:01.055
[Iblis sighs]

44:02.014 --> 44:03.390
Whether or not, at death's door,

44:03.474 --> 44:06.518
that mortal regretted
sacrificing her wishes for others.

44:06.602 --> 44:09.063
Why am I always
reclining in this position?

44:09.146 --> 44:10.731
It's so uncomfortable.

44:10.814 --> 44:13.192
Why do I only have one piece of furniture?

44:13.275 --> 44:17.154
Hundreds of years spent thinking,
obsessed with three questions.

44:18.197 --> 44:19.031
And even still--

44:19.114 --> 44:23.077
Whatever you say next,
make sure to choose your words carefully.

44:24.495 --> 44:26.246
It's still a giant mystery to me.

44:26.330 --> 44:28.707
Uh, okay. Damn it.

44:28.791 --> 44:30.626
Not the intelligent type.

44:30.709 --> 44:32.002
Don't you dare mention

44:32.086 --> 44:34.713
that her three wishes
were nobly spent on others, okay?

44:34.797 --> 44:38.801
Or about her being virtuous
in every life since and, well, everything…

44:38.884 --> 44:39.843
Never, yeah?

44:39.927 --> 44:41.637
Do not ever let the mortal know.

44:41.720 --> 44:43.514
[Sade] I wouldn't dare tell her any of it.

44:43.597 --> 44:46.975
But did you know Master's master
is standing just outside?

44:47.893 --> 44:49.186
[gasps]

44:49.937 --> 44:52.481
So… So, how much did you hear?

44:53.774 --> 44:55.776
Not the observant type either.

44:58.153 --> 44:59.363
[Iblis] Wait.

44:59.446 --> 45:01.073
Why'd you close the door?

45:02.616 --> 45:04.118
What are you dressed up for?

45:04.201 --> 45:06.412
Hey, Ki Ka-young.
Where are you going?

45:06.495 --> 45:08.163
-[car door closes]
-Ki Ka-young!

45:08.247 --> 45:09.581
[Newton's cradle ticking]

45:09.665 --> 45:11.166
YOO PSYCHIATRIC CLINIC

45:13.293 --> 45:15.087
Ms. Ki Ka-young, right this way.

45:20.717 --> 45:22.928
[romantic classical music plays]

45:28.892 --> 45:30.727
[Iblis gags and groans]

45:34.356 --> 45:37.609
Why do I have to carry all these?
I think I'm getting sick.

45:37.693 --> 45:38.652
And I'm dizzy.

45:38.735 --> 45:39.903
I've got heels on.

45:43.866 --> 45:45.868
I need a better reason than just that.

45:48.829 --> 45:49.997
What are we doing here?

45:50.789 --> 45:53.584
Normal people go out for dinner
at places like this

45:53.667 --> 45:55.335
and take photos and such.

46:04.511 --> 46:05.929
[chair scrapes]

46:06.680 --> 46:07.764
Right this way.

46:11.643 --> 46:12.478
[Iblis grunts]

46:13.937 --> 46:15.230
Hmm?

46:21.653 --> 46:22.905
Hmm? [pants]

46:25.157 --> 46:26.408
[exhales]

46:27.326 --> 46:28.327
[chuckles softly]

46:31.455 --> 46:32.289
Mm!

46:34.666 --> 46:36.001
Mm!

46:37.294 --> 46:38.378
Mm.

46:39.588 --> 46:42.925
So, the doctor's office you were at,
is that where you get your pills from?

46:43.592 --> 46:44.927
Do they help you a lot?

46:45.010 --> 46:46.553
Is that what you think?

46:46.637 --> 46:49.181
The pills are
for my grandma's peace of mind.

46:50.140 --> 46:51.141
A few are vitamins.

46:55.270 --> 46:58.524
Why? Are you hoping
there's some cure out there?

46:58.607 --> 47:01.276
Do you spend every day
wishing that you could kill me?

47:02.861 --> 47:03.820
'Cause you're Satan?

47:04.988 --> 47:06.740
-[cutlery clatters]
-[clears throat]

47:07.658 --> 47:08.825
That's not what I said.

47:10.244 --> 47:11.286
So, what, then?

47:12.246 --> 47:14.998
So you're abnormal,
where do you actually want to be?

47:23.590 --> 47:26.260
[romantic classical music playing]

47:42.192 --> 47:43.777
You're not gonna push me off this time?

47:47.906 --> 47:50.325
[romantic classical music continues]

48:03.422 --> 48:06.091
There are no cameras
this high up, are there?

48:07.968 --> 48:08.802
Not sure.

48:13.974 --> 48:15.976
I could still push you off, you know.

48:17.019 --> 48:20.439
I'll never understand
why you're always so angry.

48:20.522 --> 48:22.149
Right now, you know why.

48:25.861 --> 48:28.739
Even so, it's nice to know there's a place
where you can feel at peace.

48:28.822 --> 48:31.491
This is one nice perk
about being your master.

48:33.118 --> 48:35.287
It's dark here,
so you might not have noticed.

48:35.370 --> 48:37.164
I have no emotions.

48:38.540 --> 48:40.292
But as much as I can, I like you.

48:45.881 --> 48:46.798
Uh…

48:47.758 --> 48:50.093
Stop being… so forward.

48:55.307 --> 48:56.183
Why?

48:57.517 --> 48:58.518
Why do you like me?

48:59.227 --> 49:00.270
You're…

49:01.563 --> 49:03.315
like the cars I work on.

49:03.398 --> 49:06.818
The combustion engines,
the brake fluid, the tires.

49:07.402 --> 49:09.196
I don't need to make sense of you.

49:10.155 --> 49:11.156
You're sturdy.

49:11.907 --> 49:14.201
-And sometimes you shine.
-[chuckles]

49:14.284 --> 49:16.578
Out of everything I valued in life,

49:16.662 --> 49:19.873
-Grandma, Min-ji, the garage…
-Hmm.

49:19.956 --> 49:23.335
…my car, gamja-tang, the frogs…

49:23.418 --> 49:25.420
-The frogs?
-…dental drilling…

49:25.504 --> 49:27.798
I'd like to point out
I'm still not on the list.

49:27.881 --> 49:29.675
You're not making a very good case.

49:31.176 --> 49:32.844
[scoffs] All right.

49:33.804 --> 49:35.597
I'll try to rise up in the ranks.

49:36.890 --> 49:41.061
My dear master, tonight, we shall bask
in the darkest of midnights.

49:42.521 --> 49:44.022
[energy whirrs]

49:44.940 --> 49:45.774
[snaps fingers]

49:46.316 --> 49:48.568
[electricity thudding]

49:51.780 --> 49:52.781
[thudding subsides]

50:09.214 --> 50:12.175
Now we can finally see the stars.
[chuckles]

50:33.613 --> 50:34.948
[gasps]

50:36.450 --> 50:37.409
What?

50:39.119 --> 50:39.953
Do it.

50:42.622 --> 50:43.457
Do what?

50:43.999 --> 50:46.710
[Min-ji] When a man talks to you
about seeing the stars or whatever,

50:46.793 --> 50:48.587
then the moment is coming.

50:49.212 --> 50:50.213
It's coming.

50:51.256 --> 50:52.257
The kiss.

50:55.469 --> 50:56.928
I'll admit, I've thought about it.

50:57.554 --> 50:58.388
[scoffs]

50:58.472 --> 50:59.681
Whoa, easy now.

50:59.765 --> 51:02.017
What do you take me for? [laughs]

51:04.436 --> 51:05.437
I'm not kissing you.

51:05.520 --> 51:07.564
That's not fair. Why not?

51:07.647 --> 51:08.940
You brought the stars!

51:12.861 --> 51:13.862
Okay, then.

51:14.613 --> 51:15.447
Don't move.

51:16.364 --> 51:17.699
I'll do it.

51:19.117 --> 51:20.076
[kisses]

51:22.204 --> 51:23.997
-[swallows]
-Weird.

51:24.790 --> 51:25.832
Is this usual?

51:25.916 --> 51:27.042
No, it's just, uh--

51:27.125 --> 51:29.294
I said don't move. Let me try again.

51:40.889 --> 51:42.432
Yeah, no, it's just weird.

51:43.725 --> 51:44.768
[stumbles]

51:45.352 --> 51:46.895
Why even do this at all?

51:53.652 --> 51:55.070
[chuckling in disbelief]

51:59.324 --> 52:00.325
Wow.

52:03.328 --> 52:05.205
I really didn't want to do this.

52:09.960 --> 52:11.253
You're wrong.

52:11.336 --> 52:12.963
It's different when I do it.

52:13.046 --> 52:15.465
[pop ballad music playing]

53:06.933 --> 53:09.144
[pop ballad music continues]
